From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:23:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mediatek: mt6797-mt6351: suspend the card with
 the system

The machine driver has no power management operations, so a system
suspend leaves streams running and the codec biased. Use the ASoC
core's snd_soc_pm_ops, as other MediaTek machine drivers do.
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-mt6351.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-mt6351.c b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-mt6351.c
index 2922f01d9..7b0b614a4 100644
--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-mt6351.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-mt6351.c
@@ -318,6 +318,7 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, mt6797_mt6351_dt_match);
 static struct platform_driver mt6797_mt6351_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "mt6797-mt6351",
+		.pm = &snd_soc_pm_ops,
 #ifdef CONFIG_OF
 		.of_match_table = mt6797_mt6351_dt_match,
 #endif
-- 
2.43.0

